Sometimes, yes. ;)

You have to be willing to imagine something that doesn’t yet exist, believe it’s possible before you have proof, and act while everyone else is still measuring you against yesterday’s reality.

What’s called crazy in one frame of reference can become visionary in another.

But there’s an important distinction: imagination gives you permission to explore; reality gives you feedback.

The trick isn’t to abandon reality. It’s to refuse to mistake the limits of your current understanding for the limits of what’s possible.

First you imagine it. Then you test it. Then you make it real.

And if it works, suddenly they have another word for crazy: pioneer.